    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "STAGE_HANDOFF",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Picture a test for deleting a todo. Before you can delete one, a todo has to exist — so most people click through the whole create flow first, in the browser, every single run. But wait. Nobody's testing the create form today. That's scenery. So make the todo over the phone instead, in forty milliseconds, and only then open the page. Everything lit up here is the actual thing under test. Everything above it was just getting the stage ready.",
      "data": {
        "stageHandoff": {
          "testName": "test_delete_todo",
          "railLabel": "setup · by API",
          "stageLabel": "the test · by UI",
          "handoffLabel": "hang up. open the page.",
          "verdict": "when it fails, you know why",
          "caption": "scenery by phone. the scene on stage.",
          "color": "blue",
          "atWord": 3.417,
          "steps": [
            {
              "label": "api.post(\"/api/todos\")",
              "sub": "40ms",
              "title": "api",
              "atWord": 23.5
            },
            {
              "label": "read the new id back",
              "sub": "still no browser",
              "title": "api",
              "atWord": 27.583
            },
            {
              "label": "page.goto(\"/todos\")",
              "sub": "now we look",
              "title": "ui",
              "atWord": 37.25
            },
            {
              "label": "click Delete on the row",
              "sub": "the behaviour",
              "title": "ui",
              "atWord": 40.417
            },
            {
              "label": "expect(row).not_to_be_visible()",
              "sub": "the question",
              "title": "ui",
              "atWord": 42.833
            }
          ],
          "handoffAtWord": 33.167,
          "verdictAtWord": 45.25
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 794,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-16-api-testing_long_s11.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "In code the split is obvious once you've seen it. Top half, the phone call — post a todo, grab the id it hands back. That's your setup, and it never flakes, because there's no form and no clicking. Bottom half, the browser opens and does exactly one job: find that row, delete it, check it's gone.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "test_delete.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "two transports",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 2.583,
          "caption": "setup by API. behaviour by UI.",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "def test_delete_todo(page, api):"
            },
            {
              "text": "    # SETUP by API — never flakes",
              "detail": "the phone call",
              "sub": "no form, no clicking",
              "label": "setup",
              "atWord": 8.25
            },
            {
              "text": "    resp = api.post(\"/api/todos\","
            },
            {
              "text": "        data={\"title\": \"Doomed todo\"})",
              "detail": "a todo now exists",
              "sub": "40ms, no browser yet",
              "label": "made",
              "atWord": 14.75
            },
            {
              "text": "    todo_id = resp.json()[\"id\"]"
            },
            {
              "text": ""
            },
            {
              "text": "    # TEST by UI — the real question",
              "detail": "now the browser opens",
              "sub": "this part is the actual test",
              "label": "test",
              "atWord": 27.667
            },
            {
              "text": "    page.goto(\"/todos\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "    row = page.get_by_role(\"listitem\")"
            },
            {
              "text": "        has_text=\"Doomed todo\")",
              "detail": "find it, delete it, check it went",
              "sub": "one job, nothing else",
              "label": "done",
              "atWord": 39
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 574,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-16-api-testing_long_s12.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "BROWSER_STEP",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "And here's the bit I find genuinely satisfying. Watch the page. That todo was never typed into anything — it arrived over the phone, forty milliseconds before the browser even opened. But there it is on the list, exactly as if somebody had sat there and created it. The app can't tell the difference. Why would it? A row is a row.",
      "data": {
        "browserStep": {
          "url": "app.example.com/todos",
          "screenTitle": "Your todos",
          "caption": "seeded by phone. deleted by hand.",
          "color": "green",
          "atWord": 2.667,
          "steps": [
            {
              "text": "page.goto(\"/todos\")",
              "title": "goto",
              "label": "open the list",
              "detail": "the todos page",
              "atWord": 8.5
            },
            {
              "text": "row = get_by_role(\"listitem\")",
              "title": "check",
              "label": "there it is already",
              "detail": "Doomed todo",
              "sub": "Doomed todo",
              "atWord": 21.833
            },
            {
              "text": "row.get_by_role(\"button\").click()",
              "title": "click",
              "label": "now delete it",
              "detail": "Delete",
              "atWord": 31
            },
            {
              "text": "expect(row).not_to_be_visible()",
              "title": "assert",
              "label": "and it is gone",
              "detail": "the row",
              "sub": "gone",
              "atWord": 35.083
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 640,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-16-api-testing_long_s13.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
