    {
      "id": "s15",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "One question comes up every single time, so let's get ahead of it. What if the API needs you logged in? Almost all of them do. Well — remember that auth dot json file from last episode? The request context takes it too. Same file, same trick.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "conftest.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "an authed line",
          "color": "purple",
          "atWord": 2.667,
          "caption": "the stamp works on the phone too",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "ctx = playwright.request.new_context(",
              "detail": "the same request context",
              "sub": "still no browser anywhere",
              "label": "ctx",
              "atWord": 11.75
            },
            {
              "text": "    base_url=\"https://api.example.com\",",
              "detail": "the host, set once",
              "sub": "every call is a short path",
              "label": "base",
              "atWord": 21.75
            },
            {
              "text": "    storage_state=\"auth.json\")",
              "detail": "hand it the stamp from ep 15",
              "sub": "the API sees you logged in",
              "label": "stamp",
              "atWord": 31.667
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 488,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-16-api-testing_long_s15.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "type": "CODE_RUN",
      "transition": "push",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "narration": "Or maybe your API wants a bearer token in a header instead. There's a keyword for exactly that — extra HTTP headers. Set it once, when you build the context, and it rides along on every single call after. Then, when the run's finished, dispose of the context. That's mostly politeness, but it does close the connection properly.",
      "data": {
        "codeRun": {
          "filename": "conftest.py",
          "language": "py",
          "resultLabel": "headers + cleanup",
          "color": "purple",
          "atWord": 2.667,
          "caption": "set once. sent on every call.",
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "ctx = playwright.request.new_context(",
              "detail": "same context, built again",
              "sub": "this is still conftest.py",
              "label": "ctx",
              "atWord": 6.917
            },
            {
              "text": "    extra_http_headers={",
              "detail": "a header on every request",
              "sub": "set it exactly once",
              "label": "headers",
              "atWord": 15.333
            },
            {
              "text": "        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ...\"})",
              "detail": "whatever your API wants",
              "sub": "a token, a key, an api-key",
              "label": "token",
              "atWord": 25.5
            },
            {
              "text": "yield ctx"
            },
            {
              "text": "ctx.dispose()",
              "detail": "and hang up when you are done",
              "sub": "closes the connection",
              "label": "hang up",
              "atWord": 39
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "durationFrames": 609,
      "audio": "audio/pw-dojo-16-api-testing_long_s16.mp3",
      "timingSource": "tts"
    },
    {
